hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"231","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: My beloved friend Abul Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him) advised me regarding three things: ""Witr before sleeping, two rak‘ahs of Duha prayer, and fasting three days every month."""
"232","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: My beloved (Prophet) (peace and blessings be upon him) advised me regarding three things: ""To perform Witr before sleeping, to offer two units of Duha prayer, and to fast three days every month."""
"233","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not pray Witr is not one of us."""
"234","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) at the time of Fajr prayer: ""Bilal! Tell me about the most hopeful righteous deed you have done, and which, in your view, was for the benefit of Islam, for I heard the sound of your footsteps ahead of me in Paradise last night."" He replied: ""I do not consider any deed more hopeful to me than this: whenever I have performed ablution at any time of the night or day, I have offered as much voluntary prayer as Allah has destined for me."""
"235","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every night, in the last third of it, Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven, and a caller announces: Is there anyone who asks so that I may grant him? Is there anyone seeking forgiveness so that I may forgive him? He says this three times."""
"236","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven every night when the last third of the night remains and says: Who calls upon Me so that I may answer his supplication, who asks Me for forgiveness so that I may forgive him."""
"237","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) spent one night performing Tahajjud. When morning came, he said: ""May Allah have mercy on so-and-so, how many verses he reminded me of which I had been made to forget."""
"238","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stand in the two rak'ahs before Fajr for a duration equal to the recitation of Surah Al-Fatihah."
"239","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to only use the miswak after performing Witr, and then he would offer two light rak'ahs."
"240","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Tahajjud prayer, he used to recite this supplication: ""O Allah! All kinds of praise are for You alone, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth, all praise is for You alone, You are the Sustainer (and Manager) of the heavens and the earth, all praise is for You alone, You are the Lord of the heavens, the earth, and whatever is between them, You are the Truth, Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Your word is true, Hell is true, Paradise is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah! I have believed in You, I have submitted myself to You (in obedience), I have placed my trust in You, I have turned towards You, by Your guidance I have argued (against falsehood), and I make You my judge. You are the only One worthy of worship, there is no deity except You."""
"241","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform Tahajjud, he would supplicate: ""O Allah! All types of praise are for You alone."" Then the narrator mentioned the hadith similar to the previous one."
"242","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up during a part of the night. He used the miswak, then came to the water-skin and performed ablution. Then I got up and performed ablution. The narrator said: I do not know whether he mentioned the use of the miswak. Then I stood on his left side, so he took hold of me and turned me to stand on his right side, and he began to pass his hand over my head. Then he prayed four rak‘ahs, then prayed the witr prayer, then he prayed the two rak‘ahs (sunnah) of Fajr, and then he went out for the Fajr prayer."
